<title>USA: DirecTV says it foresees $125 million loss for '96.</title>
<headline>DirecTV says it foresees $125 million loss for '96.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>DirecTV Inc of Hughes Electronics will likely register a $125 million loss for the year, the president of the company said Tuesday.  </p>
<p>&quot;We've been operating at a loss since we began,&quot; Eddy Hartenstein told reporters attending a forum.</p>
<p>He did not give a comparative figure.</p>
<p>In June, Hartenstein told Reuters he foresaw the company breaking even in 1997.</p>
<p>Hartenstein also told reporters DirecTV planned to launch by the second half of next year a new class of multimedia services that it was developing with computer software giant Microsoft Corp.</p>
</text>
